ift in momentum. That move, which produced a daily range of roughly 75 pips on the close, effectively broke the pair out of the consolidation band that had capped price through early July, and the subsequent behaviour has been broadly supportive of the bullish read.\n\nThe structure story centres on three meaningful zones. The 0.6961 prior reaction zone \u2014 tested on four separate occasions \u2014 has transitioned from a ceiling into what now appears to be a floor, with the 23 July pullback finding buyers precisely in that vicinity before the pair recovered to close the week near 0.6998. Above current price, the 0.7183 prior reaction zone represents the next area of meaningful supply on the daily chart, though the more immediate test is whether the pair can consolidate above the psychological 0.7000 handle. The 0.6989 structure support, touched twice in recent sessions, is the level the desk is watching most closely on any near-term dip; a daily close beneath it would begin to erode the short-term bullish case.\n\nOn the H1 timeframe, the picture is one of controlled accumulation. Price spent the overnight session coiling in a narrow 0.6982\u20130.6984 range before the 05:00 candle delivered a sharp push through 0.7000, tagging 0.7007 before sellers trimmed the move. Since then, hourly candles have been oscillating either side of 0.6995\u20130.7005, suggesting the market is digesting that early-session thrust rather than reversing it. The intraday structure of higher lows from the 0.6982 base remains intact.\n\nThe calendar is empty for today, which removes the prospect of scheduled volatility triggers. That cuts both ways \u2014 there is no catalyst to accelerate a breakout above 0.7000, but equally no risk event to knock the pair back through support. In a data-vacuum session, price action is likely to remain technically driven, with liquidity conditions potentially thinning into the US afternoon.\n\nWhat would change the bullish read? A sustained hourly close back below 0.6989 structure support would suggest the recent attempt to consolidate above 0.7000 has failed, and attention would shift to the 0.6961 prior reaction zone as the next meaningful defence. A daily close beneath 0.6961 would materially weaken the higher-low sequence that has underpinned the move from June's lows.\n\nThis is editorial analysis, not financial advice. Trading involves substantial risk of loss.", "sample": false}